$WW,1$$FG,5$$TX+CX,"About THE TEMPLE OF HERMES"$$FG$

$FG,5$What this is:$FG$
THE TEMPLE OF HERMES is a public-domain operating system for a human and an
AI agent sharing one machine.  It is a rebrand and continuation of TinkerOS
5.20-rc10, which is a fork of TempleOS.  This image is version 0.1.3.

$FG,5$Lineage and credit:$FG$
* $LK,"TempleOS",A="FI:::/Doc/AboutTempleOS.DD"$ was created by $FG,2$Terry A. Davis$FG$ and is public domain.
* $LK,"TinkerOS",A="FI:::/Doc/AboutTinkerOS.DD"$ is the TempleOS-compatible base by its authors and is released under the Unlicense.
* ZealOS supplied code that TinkerOS already credits.
* Spirit is credited as prior art for a boot-time serial guest agent.

$FG,5$New in this fork:$FG$
The Hermes agent daemon on COM1, exact DolDoc text export, the presence banner
and agent cursor, the event stream, the skip-install boot, the agent-aware
input guards, and the Temple of Hermes branding and art are new work in this
fork.  They are placed in the public domain under the Unlicense.

$FG,5$Modes:$FG$
The presence banner shows USER, SHARED, or AGENT.  In AGENT mode the kernel
input gate refuses $FG,2$YorN$FG$, $FG,2$AreYouSure$FG$, $FG,2$Fmt$FG$,
$FG,2$OSInstall$FG$, and $FG,2$BootHDIns$FG$.  SHARED allows an ordinary
$FG,2$YorN$FG$ for the human but still refuses format and install.

